# The walked twin of unit_q58_batch_retained.lm2 (--walk-methods: put and Batch's procedure walked): the retained
# tree of Batch -- the one statement `put: 7` -- is executed by the walker when Batch is executed, and not at the
# definition; count reads the unit's cell through node\hits: 0 after the definition, 1 after `Batch`.  Success is 7.
int: hits 0
fn: put (int: n) int
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
    return: n
end: put
Batch: (put: 7)
fn: count () int
return: node\hits
int: before count()
Batch
int: after count()
int: ok 0
if: before = 0 && after = 1
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
